  "honest_label": "Tumour parameters (size, type, margin, lobe) come from a certified-quantum roll (job-level CHSH; simulator runs are labelled as such). Growth is a classical cellular automaton (Kansal\u2013Torquato layers + Pixel2Cancer pleura wall, calibrated to published volume-doubling times (verify)). The image is a classical 3-D insertion into a public LIDC-IDRI CT scanned on a Siemens scanner, with that scan's own measured blur and noise; lesion shape and HU come from a parameter-only library fitted to LIDC nodules (no patient voxels in the generator). The quantum bits seed growth and appearance: replayable provenance, not realism. All nodules sit in one host scan (one patient background).",
